# Wave W17-Q (Route 120): ledger sand — long-rain road sand: a grey-cool wet sand, puddle-polished harder than Route 119’s gauge sand — grey-blue sheen flecks stand in the tread in ruled pairs where the rain keeps its mirrors longest (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, Highbranch to the Lotus Cove road). Split from the gauge sand by temperature and finish: this road is colder, greyer, and shines in lines.
